The minimal change to satisfy `coreRejectsDuplicateEmail` is in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (lines 108-112): add an email-duplicate check against `existingOwners` (case-insensitive, guarding for null emails) and include it in the condition that returns `HttpStatus.CONFLICT`. Email is already lower-cased by `OwnerFieldsValidator`, so a case-insensitive compare (or plain equals on already-normalized values) will match the spec.

